#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Shared SERVE quality gate for Dialectica (built 2026-11-15 as lab
preparation after the first falsified serve answer, MEKANISME §82).

Why this module exists: the one-shot claim path has always sent its
drafts through the full wrapper gate (`openrouter_wrapper.wrap_answer`
+ the fail-closed sendable semantics of §35/§45: status OK + zero
surviving audit findings + format gate (g) LOLOS, with the §45
mechanical floor K-1/K-2 riding as FLOOR findings). The background
SERVE paths did not share that protection end to end:

- the Vyce serve ran with NO prepare hook and NO wrapper at all — the
  provider's raw model output was submitted verbatim, which is how
  ISO f0bb3586 shipped a 38,591-char thinking trace (0 URLs, 0
  citations, 557 unbound numbers) and was falsified in ±85 s;
- neither serve path verified that the target was still LIVE — the
  §82 structural finding was 11/11 sampled serve answers landing on
  questions whose marathon round had already ended
  (`marathonEligible=false`, upside $0, full downside).

This module is the single gate both serve lanes now share. It does
NOT define a second standard: the content gate is the claim wrapper
itself, reused verbatim, plus two serve-specific layers the claim
path gets from its operator instead —

1. LIVENESS (`liveness_check`): the three-field filter of
   KULIT-SISTEM-2026-11-14 edge #2 over the ISR detail —
   `marathonActive` + `marathonConcluded` + the eligible rounds'
   `endsAt`. LIVE only when a round's max `endsAt` is still in the
   future, or (no marathon dimension at all) the question is still
   open. The stale-flag pattern (concluded, every endsAt past) is
   DEAD; a marathon question with no future endsAt is DEAD
   (fail-closed); an unavailable detail is DEAD at prepare time.

2. THINKING-TRACE (`detect_thinking_trace`): mechanical detectors
   for the f0bb3586 species — a draft that is the model's raw
   reasoning monologue instead of an answer: (i) opens with a
   reasoning preamble ("Let me think about this task carefully."),
   (ii) carries first-person uncertainty monologue ("I genuinely
   don't remember…", "I really can't reproduce it reliably."),
   (iii) is dominated by a raw code dump, or (iv) closes with a plan
   ("Decision: I will structure my novel contribution around…")
   instead of delivering the answer. A trace finding has no span, so
   under the lanes' established semantics it is unpatchable and
   withholds the draft.

3. EVASIVE SOURCE CLOSING (`detect_evasive_source_closing`, E3 —
   ADOPTED by the lab of 2026-11-15, LAB-E3-SENSUS-E-2026-11-15.md
   §1.5–§1.6): an explicit source-evasion admission in the draft's
   CLOSING or SOURCE SECTION ("avoids pinpoint references", "cannot
   be verified from the text alone", "no live web access", "I give
   no URLs", …). All four falsified serve answers (f0bb3586,
   7d81c51d, 5b5e8212, a3b8b34a) closed with the same verbatim
   evasion; the measured false-positive rate is 0/203 verified
   (KORPUS-JUARA-2026-11-14). The scan is deliberately BOUNDED to
   the closing block and source sections: deferral language in the
   body (e.g. "verify exact current values in the live docs" in
   verified 0006fe08) is NOT a trigger. Like the trace layer, the
   finding has no span and withholds the draft.

SEMANTIC SELF-VFP — deliberately NOT mechanised here. On the claim
path, semantic support (operator prompt T10.2 / T12 item 5) is the
operating agent's own judgement: open every citation and point at
the sentence that supports each bound claim. It is not a model call
inside the wrapper, and the wrapper's own docstring calls it a
separate, non-delegable check (claim #1 passed every mechanical
threshold and died on support). A background serve has no agent in
the loop, so this gate cannot honestly reproduce that check:
`gate_answer` therefore reports `semantic_vfp.performed = False` on
every result, and whether serve may run on the mechanical gate alone
— or must add a semantic stage first — is an explicit lab decision
(see GERBANG-SERVE-2026-11-15.md). The gate accepts an optional
`semantic_check` callable so a lab-approved stage can be plugged in
without redesign; it ships unpopulated.

Fetch arming: reading the ISR detail needs the account session, so
`fetch_isr_detail` only touches the network when the launcher arms
it with DIALECTICA_SERVE_GATE_FETCH=1 (run_serve sets this for both
serve modes). Unarmed (unit tests, manual provider runs) it reports
state "disabled" and callers fall back as documented per call site:
prepare hooks evaluate the search row's own fields; job-time
fallbacks proceed unless death is PROVEN (a job already exists —
dropping it on an unverifiable fetch would burn reliability for
nothing; the structural gate is prepare, before any claim).
"""
